---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="The Periodic Table of Digital Matter — Simple Guide"
  description="56 building blocks of digital matter. 8 fundamental types, 7 modes. The universal structure of everything digital."
>
  <Nav />

  <main class="learn-page">

    <section class="learn-hero">
      <div class="hero-glow"></div>
      <div class="learn-hero-inner">
        <div class="badge">Simple Guide</div>
        <h1>The Periodic Table of Digital Matter</h1>
        <p class="lead">Everything digital — from code to content to models — is built from the same <strong>56 building blocks</strong>. Just like chemistry has elements, digital matter has elements too.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- English -->
    <section class="content-section" id="english">
      <div class="container">

        <div class="explainer-box">
          <h2>Why 56?</h2>
          <p>When we decompose digital matter, we find <strong>8 fundamental types</strong> and <strong>7 modes of operation</strong>. Multiply them: 8 × 7 = <strong>56 elements</strong>. Every digital entity decomposes into these 56 elements.</p>
        </div>

        <h2 class="section-title">The 8 Types of Digital Matter</h2>

        <div class="type-cards">

          <div class="type-card" style="--tc: #F72585">
            <div class="tc-header">
              <span class="tc-emoji">✅</span>
              <div>
                <div class="tc-name">Boolean</div>
                <div class="tc-color-label">Pink</div>
              </div>
              <div class="tc-tagline">Yes or No</div>
            </div>
            <p>The AI deciding: is this right or wrong?</p>
            <ul>
              <li><em>"Is 2 + 2 = 5?"</em> → No.</li>
              <li><em>"Is water wet?"</em> → Yes.</li>
              <li><em>"Should I trust this email?"</em> → Yes or No.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="tc-note">Every fact check, every safety filter — all Boolean.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="type-card" style="--tc: #00D9FF">
            <div class="tc-header">
              <span class="tc-emoji">🔢</span>
              <div>
                <div class="tc-name">Number</div>
                <div class="tc-color-label">Cyan</div>
              </div>
              <div class="tc-tagline">Counting &amp; Measuring</div>
            </div>
            <p>Anything involving amounts, sizes, or comparisons.</p>
            <ul>
              <li><em>"How many planets?"</em> → 8.</li>
              <li><em>"What's bigger — elephant or car?"</em> → Elephant.</li>
              <li><em>"How much does water weigh?"</em> → 8.34 lbs/gallon.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="tc-note">If the answer is a number, a size, or a rank — it lives here.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="type-card" style="--tc: #7209B7">
            <div class="tc-header">
              <span class="tc-emoji">🔤</span>
              <div>
                <div class="tc-name">Symbol</div>
                <div class="tc-color-label">Purple</div>
              </div>
              <div class="tc-tagline">Words, Letters, Code</div>
            </div>
            <p>The language pieces themselves — not what words mean, but what they ARE.</p>
            <ul>
              <li><em>"What does 'photosynthesis' mean?"</em></li>
              <li><em>"Is this Python code correct?"</em></li>
              <li><em>"What does '∞' represent?"</em></li>
            </ul>
            <p class="tc-note">Spelling, grammar, code syntax, abbreviations — all Symbol.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="type-card" style="--tc: #4CC9F0">
            <div class="tc-header">
              <span class="tc-emoji">👤</span>
              <div>
                <div class="tc-name">Identity</div>
                <div class="tc-color-label">Blue</div>
              </div>
              <div class="tc-tagline">Who, What, Where</div>
            </div>
            <p>Names of real things in the world: people, places, organizations.</p>
            <ul>
              <li><em>"Who is Einstein?"</em> → A physicist.</li>
              <li><em>"Where is Tokyo?"</em> → Japan.</li>
              <li><em>"Who made the iPhone?"</em> → Apple.</li>
            </ul>
            <div class="sub-table">
              <div class="sub-head">
                <span>Sub-type</span><span>What it covers</span>
              </div>
              <div class="sub-row"><span>Person</span><span>Real people</span></div>
              <div class="sub-row"><span>Organization</span><span>Companies, governments</span></div>
              <div class="sub-row"><span>Place</span><span>Countries, cities, landmarks</span></div>
              <div class="sub-row"><span>Product</span><span>Things made and sold</span></div>
              <div class="sub-row"><span>Role</span><span>Jobs and positions</span></div>
              <div class="sub-row"><span>Work</span><span>Books, movies, songs</span></div>
              <div class="sub-row"><span>General</span><span>Other named things</span></div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="type-card" style="--tc: #22C55E">
            <div class="tc-header">
              <span class="tc-emoji">🗺️</span>
              <div>
                <div class="tc-name">Space</div>
                <div class="tc-color-label">Green</div>
              </div>
              <div class="tc-tagline">Location &amp; Direction</div>
            </div>
            <p>Where things are relative to each other. Inside, outside, above, below, near, far.</p>
            <ul>
              <li><em>"Is the heart on the left or right?"</em></li>
              <li><em>"Which direction does the sun rise?"</em></li>
              <li><em>"Is Antarctica bigger than Europe?"</em></li>
            </ul>
            <p class="tc-note">Physical position, geography, spatial relationships — Space.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="type-card" style="--tc: #FFD60A">
            <div class="tc-header">
              <span class="tc-emoji">⏰</span>
              <div>
                <div class="tc-name">Time</div>
                <div class="tc-color-label">Yellow</div>
              </div>
              <div class="tc-tagline">When, How Long, Before &amp; After</div>
            </div>
            <p>Everything about timing, sequence, and dates.</p>
            <ul>
              <li><em>"When did World War II end?"</em> → 1945.</li>
              <li><em>"How long does light take from the Sun?"</em> → 8 minutes.</li>
              <li><em>"What came first — Renaissance or Industrial Revolution?"</em></li>
            </ul>
            <p class="tc-note">Dates, durations, order of events — all Time.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="type-card" style="--tc: #F59E0B">
            <div class="tc-header">
              <span class="tc-emoji">🔗</span>
              <div>
                <div class="tc-name">Relation</div>
                <div class="tc-color-label">Amber</div>
              </div>
              <div class="tc-tagline">Connections &amp; Causes</div>
            </div>
            <p>How things connect to each other. Because, therefore, part of, similar to, opposite of.</p>
            <ul>
              <li><em>"Why does ice melt in warm weather?"</em></li>
              <li><em>"What's the connection between smoking and cancer?"</em></li>
              <li><em>"What is France part of?"</em> → Europe → Earth.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="tc-note">The hardest type for AI. Requires understanding WHY, not just WHAT.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="type-card" style="--tc: #EF4444">
            <div class="tc-header">
              <span class="tc-emoji">🎲</span>
              <div>
                <div class="tc-name">Entropy</div>
                <div class="tc-color-label">Red</div>
              </div>
              <div class="tc-tagline">Uncertainty &amp; Probability</div>
            </div>
            <p>How confident is the AI? Is it guessing? Is the answer definite or just "probably"?</p>
            <ul>
              <li><em>"Will it rain tomorrow?"</em> — maybe.</li>
              <li><em>"What's the most common surname in China?"</em> — probably Wang.</li>
              <li><em>"Is this symptom serious?"</em> — possibly, see a doctor.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="tc-note">When the answer is "it depends" or "probably" — that's Entropy.</p>
          </div>

        </div>

        <!-- The 7 Laws -->
        <div class="laws-section">
          <h2 class="section-title">The 7 Ways Things Work</h2>
          <p class="laws-intro">Every type of thinking also has <strong>7 modes</strong> — ways the thinking can work. Together: 8 types × 7 modes = <strong>56 elements</strong>.</p>
          <div class="laws-grid">
            <div class="law-card">
              <div class="law-name">Distinction</div>
              <div class="law-q">"What makes this different?"</div>
            </div>
            <div class="law-card">
              <div class="law-name">Conservation</div>
              <div class="law-q">"What stays the same?"</div>
            </div>
            <div class="law-card">
              <div class="law-name">Composition</div>
              <div class="law-q">"What is it made of?"</div>
            </div>
            <div class="law-card">
              <div class="law-name">Feedback</div>
              <div class="law-q">"What happens next because of this?"</div>
            </div>
            <div class="law-card">
              <div class="law-name">Criticality</div>
              <div class="law-q">"At what point does this break?"</div>
            </div>
            <div class="law-card">
              <div class="law-name">Network</div>
              <div class="law-q">"How are these related to each other?"</div>
            </div>
            <div class="law-card">
              <div class="law-name">Complexity</div>
              <div class="law-q">"How complicated is this? Can we be sure?"</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="laws-example"><strong>Example:</strong> <em>Identity × Distinction</em> means "What makes this person/place/thing DIFFERENT from others?" — <em>Relation × Feedback</em> means "When X happened, what did it cause, and what did THAT cause?"</p>
        </div>

        <!-- 56-element grid -->
        <div class="grid-section">
          <h2 class="section-title">The Full 56-Element Grid</h2>
          <p class="laws-intro">Each cell is one element. Color = the type of thinking.</p>
          <div class="el56-table-wrap">
            <table class="el56-table">
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th></th>
                  <th>Distinction</th>
                  <th>Conservation</th>
                  <th>Composition</th>
                  <th>Feedback</th>
                  <th>Criticality</th>
                  <th>Network</th>
                  <th>Complexity</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                {[
                  {name:'Boolean', color:'#F72585', abbr:'Bo'},
                  {name:'Number',  color:'#00D9FF', abbr:'Nu'},
                  {name:'Symbol',  color:'#7209B7', abbr:'Sy'},
                  {name:'Identity',color:'#4CC9F0', abbr:'Id'},
                  {name:'Space',   color:'#22C55E', abbr:'Sp'},
                  {name:'Time',    color:'#FFD60A', abbr:'Ti'},
                  {name:'Relation',color:'#F59E0B', abbr:'Re'},
                  {name:'Entropy', color:'#EF4444', abbr:'En'},
                ].map(t => (
                  <tr>
                    <td class="row-label" style={`color:${t.color}`}>{t.name}</td>
                    {['Dis','Con','Com','Feed','Crit','Net','Comp'].map(law => (
                      <td class="el-cell" style={`background:${t.color}22; border-color:${t.color}33`}>{t.abbr}-{law}</td>
                    ))}
                  </tr>
                ))}
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Big Idea -->
        <div class="big-idea">
          <h2>The Big Idea</h2>
          <p>When we scan any digital entity, we check all 56 elements. If some are weak — that's where mistakes happen. We can fix them.</p>
          <p>Instead of saying "the system is broken," we say: <em>"The system has a weakness in <strong>Identity × Network</strong> — it loses track of how people connect in a chain of relationships."</em></p>
          <p class="big-idea-punch">That's a fixable problem. We know exactly where it is, what type it is, and how to repair it without touching anything else. <strong>That's what 56 elements gives you: a map, not just a score.</strong></p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- CTA -->
    <section class="learn-cta">
      <div class="container">
        <h2>Want a free scan of your AI model?</h2>
        <p>We'll run the full 56-element analysis and deliver a signed report by email.</p>
        <a href="/probe56#free-scan" class="btn-primary">Get your free scan report &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </section>

  </main>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .learn-page { padding-top: 64px; }

  .learn-hero {
    position: relative;
    text-align: center;
    padding: 80px 24px 60px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .hero-glow {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background: radial-gradient(ellipse 60% 50% at 50% 30%, rgba(0,217,255,0.08) 0%, transparent 60%);
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .learn-hero-inner { position: relative; z-index: 1; max-width: 720px; margin: 0 auto; }

  .badge {
    display: inline-block;
    border: 1px solid rgba(0,217,255,0.3);
    color: var(--cyan);
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    padding: 5px 14px;
    border-radius: 20px;
    margin-bottom: 24px;
    background: rgba(0,217,255,0.06);
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(32px, 6vw, 56px);
    font-weight: 900;
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
    color: #fff;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .lead {
    font-size: 18px;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: 32px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .lead strong { color: #fff; }

  .content-section { padding: 80px 24px; }
  .content-section.alt { background: var(--bg2); }

  .container { max-width: 1100px; margin: 0 auto; }

  .explainer-box {
    background: rgba(0,217,255,0.04);
    border: 1px solid rgba(0,217,255,0.15);
    border-radius: 16px;
    padding: 32px 36px;
    margin-bottom: 64px;
  }

  .explainer-box h2 {
    font-size: 24px;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: #fff;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  .explainer-box p {
    font-size: 17px;
    color: #94A3B8;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .explainer-box strong { color: var(--cyan); }

  .section-title {
    font-size: clamp(22px, 3vw, 32px);
    font-weight: 800;
    color: #fff;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    margin-bottom: 32px;
  }

  /* Type cards */
  .type-cards {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    gap: 20px;
    margin-bottom: 64px;
  }

  .type-card {
    background: var(--bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-top: 3px solid var(--tc);
    border-radius: 14px;
    padding: 24px 20px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .tc-header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 12px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .tc-emoji { font-size: 22px; line-height: 1; flex-shrink: 0; }

  .tc-name {
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--tc);
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  .tc-color-label {
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--muted);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  }

  .tc-tagline {
    margin-left: auto;
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--muted);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .type-card p {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: #94A3B8;
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .type-card ul {
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 6px;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .type-card ul li {
    font-size: 13px;
    color: #CBD5E1;
    padding-left: 16px;
    position: relative;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .type-card ul li::before {
    content: '·';
    position: absolute;
    left: 4px;
    color: var(--tc);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .tc-note {
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-style: italic;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 10px;
    margin-top: 4px;
  }

  /* Sub-table for Identity */
  .sub-table {
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    overflow: hidden;
    font-size: 12px;
    margin-top: 4px;
  }

  .sub-head, .sub-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    padding: 6px 10px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .sub-row:last-child { border-bottom: none; }

  .sub-head {
    background: rgba(76,201,240,0.08);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 11px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .sub-row { color: #94A3B8; }
  .sub-row span:first-child { color: #CBD5E1; font-weight: 600; }

  /* Laws */
  .laws-section { margin-bottom: 64px; }

  .laws-intro {
    font-size: 16px;
    color: #94A3B8;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 28px;
  }

  .laws-intro strong { color: #fff; }

  .laws-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(7, 1fr);
    gap: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 24px;
  }

  .law-card {
    background: var(--bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 16px 12px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .law-name {
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #fff;
  }

  .law-q {
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .laws-example {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: #94A3B8;
    line-height: 1.7;
    background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 16px 20px;
  }

  /* 56-element grid */
  .grid-section { margin-bottom: 64px; }

  .el56-table-wrap { overflow-x: auto; }

  .el56-table {
    border-collapse: collapse;
    width: 100%;
    min-width: 640px;
    font-size: 12px;
  }

  .el56-table th {
    padding: 10px 8px;
    text-align: center;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    color: var(--muted);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .row-label {
    padding: 10px 12px;
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    white-space: nowrap;
    border-right: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .el-cell {
    padding: 10px 6px;
    text-align: center;
    border: 1px solid transparent;
    border-radius: 4px;
    color: #CBD5E1;
    font-family: monospace;
    font-size: 11px;
  }

  /* Big idea */
  .big-idea {
    background: rgba(0,217,255,0.04);
    border: 1px solid rgba(0,217,255,0.15);
    border-radius: 16px;
    padding: 40px 36px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 16px;
  }

  .big-idea h2 {
    font-size: 24px;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: #fff;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .big-idea p {
    font-size: 16px;
    color: #94A3B8;
    line-height: 1.75;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .big-idea em { color: #CBD5E1; font-style: normal; }
  .big-idea strong { color: var(--cyan); }

  .big-idea-punch {
    font-size: 17px;
    color: #CBD5E1;
  }

  /* Learn CTA */
  .learn-cta {
    padding: 80px 24px;
    text-align: center;
    background: var(--bg2);
  }

  .learn-cta h2 {
    font-size: clamp(24px, 4vw, 36px);
    font-weight: 800;
    color: #fff;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
  }

  .learn-cta p {
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: 32px;
  }

  .btn-primary {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--cyan), #0099BB);
    color: #080A18;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 16px;
    padding: 14px 32px;
    border-radius: 10px;
    text-decoration: none;
    display: inline-block;
    transition: opacity 0.2s;
  }

  .btn-primary:hover { opacity: 0.85; text-decoration: none; }

  @media (max-width: 1100px) {
    .type-cards { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }
    .laws-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); }
  }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .type-cards { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .laws-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }
    .explainer-box, .big-idea { padding: 24px 20px; }
  }
</style>
